{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXjQrT5654SF7pKyXZ9T","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found two minor issues and no correctness bugs. Both are written to `.nightralph/findings.md`.\n\nThis range only changes `test/index.ts` and `AGENTS.md`. The class and `aria-label` code was already on the branch before it. I checked that code against the spec and found nothing that diverges. The browser suite passes all 107 tests, and lint reports no errors.\n\nThe findings:\n\n1. **A test assertion can never fail** (`test/index.ts:806`). The swap test compares `el.ariaLabel` with `el.button.getAttribute('aria-label')`, but the getter returns exactly that expression, so the check passes whatever the swapped button has. The test message says the replaced button \"has no label\", yet nothing checks that. It should assert that the button has no `aria-label` and that `el.ariaLabel` is `null`.\n2. **`AGENTS.md` gives the tapout port-collision rule twice**: under \"Button tests\" (lines 37-39) and under the new \"Running the browser suite\" (lines 51-55). The two copies could drift apart if only one is edited later; one copy should be dropped.\n\nThe new `AGENTS.md` notes are accurate. `test/package-version.js` does pin the literal `0.0.55`, and that is one step past v0.0.54, the latest version in `CHANGELOG.md`. The lightningcss problem the new notes describe also happens in this worktree: `npm test` stopped at `build-css` with `This: command not found`. So I ran the browser suite directly with `esbuild test/index.ts --bundle | tapout`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1074,"cache_read_input_tokens":51722,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1074},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagno